    "type": "question",
    "label": "55",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$(x^2+1)^4-3(x^2+1)^2-54=0.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\pm\\sqrt2$.\n\nLet $u=(x^2+1)^2$ and reject branches inconsistent with $x^2+1>0$.",
      "worked": "Let $u=(x^2+1)^2\\ge1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-3u-54&=0\\\\(u-9)(u+6)&=0\\\\u&=9\\text{ or }u=-6.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $u=-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^2+1)^2&=9\\\\x^2+1&=\\pm3.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $x^2+1>0$, retain only the positive branch.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+1&=3\\\\x^2&=2\\\\x&=\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
